WEBVTT

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.980
I'm going to run in the Hakone Ekiden.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.700
Starting today, I'm going
to win over all the guys.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.350
That includes you,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.780
Sendai Josei High School graduate,

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.180
Kurahara Kakeru.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.800
Just who are you?

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.140
There, there.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.590
You must be hungry.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.100
Let's head back. Time for breakfast.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.990
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.320
We can't.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.330
Not Hakone.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.370
There's no way.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.790
No one knows that for sure.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.830
I know.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:38.450
The top track and field teams
train every day for years,

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.060
but only a handful of them even qualify.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.600
That's the kind of race it is.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.320
You know a lot about Hakone Ekiden?

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.690
Don't worry.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.500
Dreams do come true if you try.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.860
Nico-chan Senpai has 
track and field experience.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:02:59.990
What?

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.870
Yuki made it to a prefectural
kendo tournament with his team.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:07.280
The twins and King played soccer
for three years in high school.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:13.380
Shindo used to walk ten kilometers through
the mountains to get to school and back everyday.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.240
That's not a sport.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.090
And Musa has a hidden talent.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:23.340
It's prejudiced to think 
black people are fast runners.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:27.130
I confirmed in the bath
 that you've got good muscles.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:29.110
That's why you're always staring at me?

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.740
Then there's Kurahara.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:34.520
I want you guys to see how he runs.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:40.250
Excuse me, but I wasn't included just now.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.220
In other words, I don't have to run—

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.240
We finally have ten.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.060
Apparently, you're included.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.270
I'm not going to run with you guys.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.570
<b><i>The Ogre's Arrival</i></b>

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:44.930
Kurahara, there's an open seat there.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:45.700
Huh?

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.680
Latecomers sit over there.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:54.360
Have as many helpings as you'd like.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.320
Thanks for the food.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.280
You're welcome.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.860
That chair's mine.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.650
<b>Chikusei-so Cleaning Duty Schedule</b>

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.300
I'm going to clean the toilets.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.160
Thanks.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.480
I'm going to feed Nira.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:31.310
No one's going along with Haiji's plan, right?

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:35.650
That thing he mentioned yesterday? Yeah, right.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:37.850
There's no way. Absolutely not.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.610
Oh, really? Good.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:45.070
I was going to run away
if you guys said you'd do it.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.780
It's too sudden.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.830
It's a scam.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.740
What did Musa say?

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.820
Between school and work, he's too busy.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:57.070
So everyone's against it.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.720
Got it, newbie?

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:02.110
But...

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:05.590
I doubt he'd just back down.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:10.590
These are the most luxurious dishes
we've been served all month.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:16.050
He's domesticated us, hasn't he?

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:22.000
I know, Kakeru. We're going to school today.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:22.850
Wanna join us?

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:23.570
Huh?

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.750
We thought we'd check things out
before the entrance ceremony.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.240
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:36.550
Joji, they've got a soccer club.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:40.440
Yeah, there's about five.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:42.670
I don't know which to join.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.500
You're going to keep playing soccer?

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:46.670
Huh?

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:50.350
Well, you heard what Haiji said.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:52.580
That makes it harder to play.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:55.720
Who cares if you want to play soccer?

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.180
It's not that we want to play soccer.

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:00.640
The problem is the girls.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.340
What?

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.430
Who doesn't love a cute manager?

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.870
Hey, the futsal team is co-ed!

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:07.610
Seriously? Let's go!

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.570
<b>Manga Club</b>

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:10.120
We are the manga club.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.240
We hope you'll consider joining us.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.420
We're accepting new members.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.930
Want to join the club?

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.580
In that case, write your name—

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.540
You seem energetic.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.420
Could you not stand there?

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:33.680
It won't be easy for you to pack,
so I thought I'd tell you first.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:35.220
Pack?

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:41.850
Apparently, you can't stay at Aotake
if you're not on the track and field team.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:46.930
In other words, if you refuse 
to be on the team, you have to move—

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:48.230
You're kicking me out?

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:51.240
No, no. Careful how you phrase it.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.130
I'm just saying you can't
live there if you don't ru—

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.010
You're kicking me out!

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:57.310
I guess you could say that.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:02.080
It'll cost a fortune to move all that stuff.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:06.030
But you don't have to leave
if you join the team.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.670
<b>Placement Office</b>

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:13.130
<b>Take a Job Fitness Exam</b>

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:13.130
<b>Eligible subjects</b>

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:13.130
<b>University students</b>

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:13.130
<b>Details</b>

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.130
<b>Use your computer to:</b>

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.130
<b>1) Receive an evaluation 3) Find the right job</b>

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.130
<b>2) Search for job information 4) Plan your career</b>

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:13.130
<b>You'll get to experience all four steps in choosing a job.</b>

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.140
Looking for a job, huh?

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:23.130
What kind of a job do you want?

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.730
Why should I tell you?

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.880
Mass media, right?

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.490
You already know.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.780
I bet you could talk about
the Ekiden at interviews.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.090
It's not something everyone gets to experience.

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:37.990
It'll help.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:53.030
There wasn't a Mountain God this year.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.420
<b>University Ekiden Final Summary</b>

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.360
Well, they can't name one every year.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:57.890
It'd reduce its value.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:02.380
Um, Haiji. This is the library.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:03.400
Keep it down.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:04.840
Shindo, how about where you're from?

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:06.230
Your hometown.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.830
It's pretty mountainous, right?

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:11.260
What's more treacherous? That or Hakone?

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.490
I've never compared them...

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.210
You haven't been home recently, right?

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.570
You ever call home?

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.660
Haiji, keep it down.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:24.460
I'm sure your family 
would be delighted if they saw

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:27.710
the son they rarely see
energetically running on TV.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.140
It's time. I gotta go.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.870
Excuse me.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.470
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:46.850
<b>102</b>

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:50.610
<b>104</b>

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.670
Nico-chan Senpai.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:05.370
You robbing me?

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:07.580
No...

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:09.640
Your cigarettes.

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:10.470
Huh?

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:13.090
I couldn't smell them.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.550
Oh, that's because I was out.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:16.510
Oh.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.290
Later.

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.680
Going to the club again?

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.490
Lawyers sure have got it easy.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:26.560
You should hurry up and graduate.

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:55.160
No way.

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:06.680
You should definitely join us.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.680
<b>Soccer Club</b>

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:06.680
Sounds really fun.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:07.750
Right?

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.540
Maybe I'll join.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:09.180
Seriously?

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.890
Well? Think you'll enjoy your student life?

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.780
If you're looking for a special-event
club, I can introduce you to one.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:21.240
It's an option if you're looking
to experience college life.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.870
You sure? You could run.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.530
No one will criticize you.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.670
If I want to run, I'll run alone.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.900
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.350
What?!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.400
I'm sorry!

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.970
Why are you running?

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:08.540
I went to work early after dropping in
on the new student symposium...

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:08.540
<b>Kobori Butcher Shop</b>

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.000
Thanks for buying so much.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.090
No, thank you for accommodating me.

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.210
Oh, it's no problem.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.910
Musa always works so hard.

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:23.190
And you're a regular. We really appreciate you.

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:24.980
I'm not that special.

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:29.000
Anyway, I'm glad I introduced him to you.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:32.250
He's such a hard worker.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:35.150
Heard that? Way to go, Musa.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.070
She's complimenting you.

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:40.610
Th-Thank you...

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:43.600
You've got a great friend.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.030
You should be grateful you met him.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.500
That's a friend for life.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.620
Hear that, Musa? We're friends for life.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.040
Musa... Musa...

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.460
He asked me what my plans
were for tomorrow morning,

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.400
and I responded that I wasn't busy...

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:01.250
He knew you couldn't say no.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:04.720
He's going after our weaknesses.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.930
What are your excuses?

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:12.720
He said it would help me find a job...

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.640
It's good for my health... like weight loss?

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:18.650
What's it really? What deals
did you make with him?

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.190
I didn't make a deal!

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.600
I really have been gaining weight lately.

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:26.530
Damn! I shouldn't have
let you go off on your own.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:30.410
Well, at least you're better than these two.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.250
It's not fair. Right, Jota?

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:38.630
Yeah. We thought everyone 
had promised to run in the Ekiden.

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:42.840
Did you listen until 
Haiji was finished talking?

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.190
He said everyone was running.

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:48.800
So we said we would, too.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.810
You're getting mites everywhere!

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:56.210
But we thought we'd give it a shot, right?

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:58.610
Yeah! Did you guys know?

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:01.100
Girls love guys who run in the Ekiden!

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:08.490
That's only true of a handful of top finishers!

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:11.410
There's no way we'll even qualify!

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.220
Huh? What does that mean?

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.640
You mean we can't just sign up for it?

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.850
I don't even feel like explaining it.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:19.080
No way!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.240
He said girls would love us!

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:22.240
The girls!

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:24.060
No one told me that!

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:25.590
Are the others okay?

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:27.510
Who's not here?

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:30.250
Nico-chan, Prince, and the newbie.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:33.510
<b>103</b>

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.270
Kakeru, are you in there?

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:36.180
Kakeru.

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:39.240
Maybe he's not back yet.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.940
I can't believe it broke now.

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:54.120
It's a miracle... my heart... didn't stop...

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:57.840
Sorry, but you can't use 
our bathroom until it's fixed.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.320
There's the Tsuru-no-yu Bathhouse.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:01.530
You'll have to go there for a while.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.020
This way.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:19.100
You sure? You could run.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:21.270
No one will criticize you.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.570
It's just for a change of pace.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:45.660
Don't tell the guys at Aotake.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:49.260
Doesn't look like you're going back, though.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.520
Do you actually want to run?

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:53.590
You idiot!

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:56.120
I said it's for a change of pace.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:59.520
They're pitch black. There's no way.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.470
Besides, I'm not cut out for it.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.190
You know a lot about running, right?

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:09.530
You ever seen a runner 
as rough around the edges as me?

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:13.950
Hey, it's them.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.130
Hey!

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:18.650
The bath's broken!

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.500
Come with us.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.130
I'll take you someplace fun before you leave.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.590
<b>Tsuru-no-yu</b>

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:27.590
I can't do it!

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:32.260
That feels great.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:34.220
It's so cool.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.720
Hell on earth.

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:39.600
That's what we call this place.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:47.250
You don't often hang out with the newbie.

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.740
Jota, let's go!

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.210
Cut that out!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.120
Oh...

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:02.080
You're all here.

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:07.660
An ogre has arrived in hell!

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:14.570
What? The landlord's bath broke?

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:16.290
Surely Haiji didn't...

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.970
Don't say it. I don't want to think about it.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:22.610
Well, Kurahara? Nice bathhouse, right?

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:25.510
Everyone else thinks it's too hot, though.

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:27.480
So do you.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:30.100
You're never in for more than a minute.

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:31.770
You're here.

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:32.690
Oh, excuse me.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:36.540
Haiji, are these guys...

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.990
Yes. They're the residents of Aotake.

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:40.490
I see.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:44.730
So you've finally got ten.

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:45.680
No.

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:49.660
I'm not a resident.

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:57.430
I met him after I left yesterday.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.130
He's new, huh?

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:00.090
I said I'm not—

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:01.300
Let's have a contest.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.000
What?

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.230
To see who can stay in the bath longer.

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:05.100
What?

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:09.600
The loser does whatever the winner says.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:14.230
You don't have to accept his challenge, Kurahara.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.490
If you refuse, I'll assume you're running away.

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:19.960
If you want to run, then run.
I won't keep chasing you.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.470
After all, you're fast...

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:24.840
...when you're running away.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:32.960
It's been three minutes.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:36.550
Hey, don't push yourselves too hard.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:43.470
You heard him.

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:47.050
Feel free to get out first.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:50.150
Haiji's tenacity is amazing.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:54.330
He's a fourth-year. It's his last year.

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:56.400
Why are you getting so sentimental?

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.740
You're not going to run with him, are you?

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:02.820
Four minutes.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.700
Yuki, why don't we have our own contest?

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:08.500
Huh?

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:10.710
We'll bet on who wins.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:13.610
If you win, I'll do whatever you want.

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:16.420
What? That's not fair.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:17.920
Hurry up.

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:26.280
The newbie, then.

00:19:26.670 --> 00:19:29.200
Are you even trying to win?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.580
Water! Water, water!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.710
Hang in there, guys!

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.210
Why'd you have to be so stubborn?

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.300
Not bad, newbie.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.940
What do we do in the case of a tie?

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:09.830
That was disgraceful.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.720
He's been waiting a long
time to get all ten guys.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:22.200
I think he's reckless, but I've
been watching him for four years.

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:26.070
He always follows through 
when he says he'd do something.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:30.580
In that case, can I make him give up?

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:35.360
Can I make him give up?

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:40.230
I don't know what happened, but go ahead.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:41.820
It'll make things easier for me.

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:45.940
Wait! I've still got time, right?

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:51.250
Sure, but it's better to start packing early.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.070
Right?

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.160
Someone help!

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:57.890
It's an ogre!

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:42.460
Next time: "A Single Flower."

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:44.920
<b>Next Time: A Single Flower</b>
